# Supabase Conventions

## Schema changes

- Add migrations as numbered SQL files in `supabase/migrations/`
- Every tenant table must have `company_id` referencing `companies(id)`
- Enable RLS on all public tables; policies must cover superadmin + company_admin scopes
- Use helper functions `current_user_role()` and `current_user_company_id()` for policies
- Animal photos: `animal_photos` + private Storage bucket `animal-photos` (path `{company_id}/{animal_id}/{id}.ext`)
- Locations → encampments hierarchy; animals link via `encampment_id`. Farm admins manage locations/encampments; all farm users can read and assign animals
- Animal inoculations: `animal_inoculations` (name, administered_at, optional next_due_at / batch / dosage)
- Demo tools (superadmin RPCs): `seed_farm_demo_data`, `clear_farm_demo_data`, `reset_farm_data` — livestock/locations only; `is_demo` flag marks seeded rows

## Auth & profiles

- `profiles` extends `auth.users`; auto-created by `handle_new_user` trigger
- Superadmin: `role = 'superadmin'`, `company_id = null`
- Company users: require `company_id`; roles `company_admin` or `company_user`
- Create users via Dashboard (with metadata) or `create-user` Edge Function — not raw SQL unless identity row is included

## User metadata for Dashboard creation

```json
{"full_name":"Name","role":"superadmin"}
```

## Edge Functions

- `supabase/functions/create-user/` — invite by email (`inviteUserByEmail`); no password; validates caller role; uses service role server-side
- `supabase/functions/delete-user/` — deletes auth user (+ cascaded profile); superadmin any user, company_admin same-company only; cannot delete self
- Invitees set password via `/reset-password` (redirect URL must be allowlisted in Supabase Auth)
- Deploy: `npx supabase functions deploy create-user` and `npx supabase functions deploy delete-user`

## Diagnostics

- `supabase/diagnose_users.sql` — check auth.users + identities + profiles alignment
- `supabase/fix_dashboard_user_creation.sql` — fix trigger if Dashboard user creation fails
